\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.6}{\ignorespaces The AntiphonyClassifier (v14) neural architecture: raw turns undergo batched utterance encoding, masked mean-pooling, and role-pure splitting ($R=20$). Persuader and Decider streams pass through independent 2-layer Transformers. The Decider stream queries the Persuader stream via directional cross-attention. Contextualized Decider states are aggregated in parallel by a commitment-trajectory GRU (read at the true final Decider turn) and attention pooling, followed by latent concatenation and Class-Balanced Focal classification.}}{28}{figure.caption.17}\protected@file@percent }
